  "profile": {
    "video_id": "iron-snail:8vtFJhMEnfE",
    "purpose": "Review of Graph Zero Japanese denim jeans sold by Denimio, part of a series on the best Japanese denim under $200. It covers fit, fabric, construction details and stitching.",
    "video_type": "review",
    "thesis": "The creator reviews Graph Zero jeans as a fully Japan-made pair under $200, set against the many Japanese denim options at higher prices. He goes through their fit, fabric and features, and gives a verdict on value and on who the cotton stitching suits.",
    "key_takeaways": [
      "Graph Zero jeans are sold through Denimio, are made in Japan and cost under $200.",
      "Fit is fairly tapered; the creator advises going true to size and never sizing down with denim.",
      "The denim is about 16 oz, unsanforized and unsinged, then rinsed by Denimio, so it should shrink only about 2%.",
      "Features include reinforced herringbone back pocket bags, a Made in Japan patch, copper rivets including on pocket bag corners, what look like iron-capped buttons, and a Levi's-style back tab.",
      "The stitching is all-cotton thread rather than poly-cotton or polyester, which gives more aging and repair character but less durability.",
      "The creator weighs value against pricier Japanese denim and sale options."
    ],
    "outline": [
      {
        "title": "Introduction to Graph Zero and Japanese denim",
        "summary": "Introduces Graph Zero jeans from Denimio as a continuation of the best Japanese denim series, with a focus on fully Japan-made jeans under $200. Mentions other brands to be covered later.",
        "first_segment": 0,
        "last_segment": 1
      },
      {
        "title": "Contest and updates",
        "summary": "Promotes the $800 Carrot contest and gives an update on delayed Iron Snail prologue jackets, with refund and bonus options. Also shows off Huckberry Portland boots.",
        "first_segment": 1,
        "last_segment": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Fit and sizing",
        "summary": "Describes the tapered fit and recommends going true to size, since the rinsed unsanforized denim shrinks about 2%. Gives the creator's height, weight and size.",
        "first_segment": 2,
        "last_segment": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Denim fabric analysis",
        "summary": "Explains the 16 oz fabric, an untranslated term the creator works out as meaning 'hair', and the unsanforized, unsinged denim with neps. Discusses value against more expensive and on-sale jeans.",
        "first_segment": 3,
        "last_segment": 5
      },
      {
        "title": "Features and contest",
        "summary": "Says the jeans carry almost every fancy Japanese denim feature at their price, then gives a longer explanation of how to enter the Carrot contest.",
        "first_segment": 5,
        "last_segment": 7
      },
      {
        "title": "Pocket bags, patch and rivets",
        "summary": "Covers reinforced herringbone back pocket bags, the Made in Japan / pride of Japan patch, and copper rivets, including rivets reinforcing the pocket bag corners.",
        "first_segment": 7,
        "last_segment": 8
      },
      {
        "title": "Buttons and branding",
        "summary": "Discusses what appear to be iron-capped buttons with copper ones elsewhere, compared with Naked & Famous MIJ full iron buttons. Also covers the Levi's-style back tab.",
        "first_segment": 9,
        "last_segment": 10
      },
      {
        "title": "Stitching and conclusion",
        "summary": "Explains the all-cotton stitching compared with poly-cotton and polyester thread, and the trade-off between durability and aging or repairability. Ends with the overall verdict.",
        "first_segment": 10,
        "last_segment": 12
      }
    ],
